1
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:06,910
Gentlemen, Star Wars day is rapidly approaching.

2
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,830
We should finalize our plans.

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:10,900
What? That's a real thing?

4
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:14,280
What is it, Star Wars Christmas?

5
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:16,680
No. Don't be ridiculous.

6
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:19,130
That's Wookiee Life Day.

7
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,210
So, when is it?

8
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:23,930
Uh, well, it's not May the fifth...

9
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:26,850
and it's not May the third...

10
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:33,680
It's May the fourth.

11
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:36,120
Get it?

12
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:40,080
May the fourth be with you?

13
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:43,100
"May the force be with you." Get it?

14
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,820
Oh, no. This face wasn't because I didn't get it.

15
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:14,350
Come in.

16
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:19,170
- Hey, you got a second? - Yes.

17
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:20,960
Actually, I'm glad you're here.

18
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:23,710
I-I'm working on the Star Wars Day schedule.

19
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:27,550
Now, I have a window built in after Phantom Menace,

20
00:01:27,550 --> 00:01:30,840
for complaining, but...

21
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:34,700
I'm worried an hour won't be enough time.

22
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:40,120
Sheldon, I-I've got some bad news.

23
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:42,170
What is it?

24
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,380
I just read online

25
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:47,350
that Arthur Jeffries passed away.

26
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,360
Professor Proton is dead?

27
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:53,880
Sorry, buddy.

28
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,380
What are you doing?

29
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:09,320
Comforting you?

30
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:11,600
Y-Your heart might be in the right place,

31
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:14,690
but your head, chest and arms certainly aren't.

32
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:18,840
Anyway, the-the funeral's on Sunday.

33
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,140
But, that's Star Wars Day.

34
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:23,330
Yeah... um...

35
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:25,590
of all the things about this that are sad,

36
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:28,300
that might not be number one.

37
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,040
You okay? I know he meant a lot to you.

38
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:34,480
I'm fine.

39
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:37,300
Okay.

40
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,570
Yet he cried when they changed the Raisin Bran box.

41
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:47,690
This, uh, this is something interesting boys and girls.

42
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:51,300
After an owl eats, he spits up part of his meal,

43
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:55,440
that he can't digest, in the form of a pellet.

44
00:02:57,710 --> 00:03:00,110
Is-Isn't that a hoot?

45
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:08,630
We'll be right back after I fire my writers.

46
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,880
Oh, shut up.

47
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:14,740
Watching your old friend?

48
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:16,530
Yes.

49
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:17,950
Look at him, Amy.

50
00:03:17,950 --> 00:03:19,670
It's such a shame.

51
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:23,080
Struck down in the prime of my life.

52
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,140
Do you want me to go to the funeral with you?

53
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:29,120
Oh, I'm not going to the funeral.

54
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,460
Why not?

55
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:33,220
All those people blowing their noses.

56
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:36,310
You can't tell the sick from the sad. Mm.

57
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:40,760
I'll be at home celebrating Star Wars Day, as planned.

58
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:43,560
Are you sure you don't want to go say good-bye?

59
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:49,080
Amy, mourning the inevitable is a complete waste of time.

60
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,120
And watching a bunch of goofy space movies

61
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:53,840
you've seen hundreds of times isn't?

62
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:56,310
If we were in a physical relationship,

63
00:03:56,310 --> 00:03:58,770
you just lost sex tonight.

64
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:02,850
Hey, guys.

65
00:04:02,850 --> 00:04:05,480
Hey, Penny. Happy Star Wars Day.

66
00:04:07,490 --> 00:04:08,960
Okay.

67
00:04:09,730 --> 00:04:10,990
Can I make you breakfast?

68
00:04:10,990 --> 00:04:15,270
Admiral Ackbar's Snack Bar is open for business.

69
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:17,940
No, thanks. Leonard and I are just going to the funeral.

70
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:19,670
You sure. Not even coffee?

71
00:04:19,670 --> 00:04:22,070
We have R2-Decaf.

72
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,390
Maybe a nice Cafe Au Leia?

73
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:28,150
And if you're not in the mood for coffee,

74
00:04:28,150 --> 00:04:31,140
I can always make you a Chai Tea-3PO.

75
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:35,060
Oh, I get it-- like C-3PO.

76
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:37,180
What happened to me?

77
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,970
Hey, uh, Sheldon, you want anything?

78
00:04:39,970 --> 00:04:41,670
Uh, no, thank you.

79
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:43,300
You're being so quiet.

80
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:46,620
Are you upset or are you just rebooting?

81
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:48,800
I'm fine.

82
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:49,900
Sweetie, are you sure you don't want to

83
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:51,740
come with us to the funeral?

84
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:54,990
Oh, I appreciate the offer, but Arthur is gone

85
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:57,050
and there's nothing I can do about it.

86
00:04:57,050 --> 00:04:59,440
When Darth Vader struck down Obi-Wan,

87
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:02,370
did Luke cry like a baby and go to his funeral?

88
00:05:02,370 --> 00:05:03,040
No.

89
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,080
He blew up the Death Star.

90
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,890
Why do I know this?!

91
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:09,250
Arthur Jeffries was a scientist.

92
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:10,910
I'm sure he didn't care about

93
00:05:10,910 --> 00:05:13,310
silly superstitions like funerals.

94
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,820
You know, if he were here, I think he'd say,

95
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:17,210
"Enjoy Star Wars Day."

96
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:20,180
He was 84; he'd say, "where's my pudding?"

97
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:24,560
Before you go, at least let me pack you some

98
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:27,580
Attack of the Scones for the road.

99
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,380
Oh, like Attack of the Clones.

100
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,320
We are leaving right now.

101
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:37,150
Arthur passing away was harder on Sheldon

102
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:38,630
than he's ready to admit.

103
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:40,440
Really hoping this will cheer him up.

104
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,850
Me, too.

105
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:43,360
Although, it might've been thoughtless of us

106
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,840
to bake a Death Star cake.

107
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:49,460
No, it combines two of Sheldon's favorite things:

108
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:50,500
chocolate chips

109
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:53,440
and the ability to destroy a planet at the push of a button.

110
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:57,260
Well, anyway, it'll be a nice surprise for the boys.

111
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,270
And Howie doesn't think I take his interests seriously,

112
00:05:59,270 --> 00:06:02,170
so hopefully this will keep him fooled for a while.

113
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:06,180
Okay, let's get the fondant and start decorating.

114
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,580
This is pretty cool.

115
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:10,110
You don't see too many spherical cakes.

116
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:15,680
I wonder why that is.

117
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,680
I have a confession to make.

118
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:26,140
I've never been to a funeral before.

119
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:27,050
Really?

120
00:06:27,050 --> 00:06:29,400
I just never knew anyone that died.

121
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:31,480
I had a pet pig when I was a kid.

122
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,690
I mean, when he died, we didn't have a funeral,

123
00:06:33,690 --> 00:06:35,180
we had a barbecue.

124
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:42,090
Yeah, we won't be eating Arthur tonight.

125
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:48,320
I didn't know him very well, but I still really liked him.

126
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:51,290
It's weird that he's... just gone.

127
00:06:51,290 --> 00:06:52,500
I know.

128
00:06:53,650 --> 00:06:55,190
I feel like I want to cry.

129
00:06:55,190 --> 00:06:57,510
Oh... that's-that's fine.

130
00:06:57,510 --> 00:06:59,220
Go ahead.

131
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:06,920
- I can't do it with you staring at me. - Sorry.

132
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:13,270
No, I'm dry.

133
00:07:13,270 --> 00:07:15,680
You're a big crybaby-- you start, I'll join in.

134
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:18,340
I am not a crybaby.

135
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:19,480
Toy Story 3?

136
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,910
The toys were holding hands in a furnace!

137
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:31,140
Look, A-Arthur lived a full life.

138
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:33,920
And he inspired a lot of people.

139
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:37,070
Sure, he-he was my childhood hero,

140
00:07:37,070 --> 00:07:40,650
but... the fact that I got to work with him,

141
00:07:40,650 --> 00:07:42,930
side by side, before he...

142
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:45,320
died was...

143
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:49,320
it was... it was a gift.

144
00:07:49,830 --> 00:07:52,020
It was a gift.

145
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:54,200
Thank you for being the emotional one

146
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,210
in this relationship.

147
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:59,990
- I got your back. - Yeah.

148
00:08:02,470 --> 00:08:04,720
Okay, here we go.

149
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,460
Episode I-- The Phantom Menace.

150
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:09,200
Let's get this over with.

151
00:08:09,610 --> 00:08:11,610
Since we all agree Episode I isn't our favorite,

152
00:08:11,610 --> 00:08:13,090
maybe we just skip it this time.

153
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:15,510
Yeah, Howard, I think you of all people

154
00:08:15,510 --> 00:08:17,140
should avoid espousing the principle

155
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:18,640
that if something is not our favorite

156
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,720
we should just get rid of it.

157
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:25,940
You know, I heard this way of watching the movies

158
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:29,450
called the Machete Order, where you watch Episodes IV and V,

159
00:08:29,450 --> 00:08:31,270
then skip Episode I,

160
00:08:31,270 --> 00:08:33,370
watch II and III as a flashback,

161
00:08:33,370 --> 00:08:35,080
and then finish with VI.

162
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:37,160
Okay, so you'd lose most of Jar Jar,

163
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:40,060
all the trade route talk, and the boring senate hearings,

164
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:43,230
which are like watching C-SPAN with monsters.

165
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:45,670
Get rid of the trade route part?

166
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:47,620
Then how would Palpatine

167
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,070
get Chancellor Valorum kicked out of office?

168
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:52,820
How would he get himself elected? How?

169
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:54,270
Can we get through one holiday

170
00:08:54,270 --> 00:08:56,390
without you saying something ridiculous?

171
00:08:57,490 --> 00:08:58,800
It was just a suggestion.

172
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,990
Well, you know what else was just a suggestion?

173
00:09:00,990 --> 00:09:03,160
"Why don't we change the Raisin Bran box?"

174
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:05,820
Hmm? And you know who got hurt by that?

175
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:08,490
Every single person who eats breakfast!

176
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,680
I think he's taking this Professor Proton thing pretty hard.

177
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:19,290
Should we try to console him?

178
00:09:19,290 --> 00:09:22,680
Or... should we respect his privacy

179
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:25,290
in this moment of grief?

180
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:27,390
By staying here and watching the movie.

181
00:09:27,390 --> 00:09:29,180
That's what good friends would do!

182
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:37,680
Well, at least without Sheldon here,

183
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,920
we got to start with Episode IV.

184
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,610
Mm, true.

185
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:45,290
I do feel guilty about him.

186
00:09:45,290 --> 00:09:46,170
Me, too.

187
00:09:46,170 --> 00:09:47,610
Maybe we should see how he's doing.

188
00:09:47,610 --> 00:09:48,170
Yeah.

189
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:50,660
- But after the cantina scene. - Obviously.

190
00:09:58,130 --> 00:09:59,830
Look at Arthur...

191
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:02,730
cracking up at a joke I told him.

192
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:08,360
I'll never hear that laugh again.

193
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,910
You never heard it that time.

194
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,550
Arthur!

195
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:20,030
- I thought you were dead. - I am.

196
00:10:20,030 --> 00:10:23,020
Oh, it-it's fantastic.

197
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:27,330
I mean, this is the longest that I've gone

198
00:10:27,330 --> 00:10:33,260
without running into a men's room in-in years.

199
00:10:34,530 --> 00:10:35,980
Why are you here?

200
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:38,300
I-I don't know. I was...

201
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:42,740
I was hoping I was going to haunt my ex-wife.

202
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:46,330
I know why.

203
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:48,850
You've come to me because

204
00:10:48,850 --> 00:10:51,710
you're my Obi-Wan.

205
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:55,170
I'm-I'm not... I'm not familiar with that.

206
00:10:55,170 --> 00:10:58,260
Is... is-is that an...

207
00:10:58,260 --> 00:11:00,570
an Internet?

208
00:11:03,210 --> 00:11:04,140
Wow.

209
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:07,830
Uh, you're dead, so I'm going to let that slide.

210
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:11,790
Obi-Wan Kenobi is a character from Star Wars.

211
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:13,740
After his physical demise,

212
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:18,710
he comes to Luke Skywalker as his mentor in spirit form.

213
00:11:19,270 --> 00:11:22,650
Well, that... that clears that up.

214
00:11:24,170 --> 00:11:27,010
You must be here to give me advice.

215
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:35,010
Well, this... this is weird.

216
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:38,540
Most-most of my robes open in...

217
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:40,270
in the back.

218
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:45,730
Those are your Jedi robes.

219
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:49,620
Oh, wait. What...?

220
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:51,770
What-what... what is this?

221
00:11:51,770 --> 00:11:54,540
Oh! Be careful with that!

222
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:09,050
Oh, neato.

223
00:12:14,170 --> 00:12:18,690
I'm, uh... I'm going to need a Band-Aid.

224
00:12:22,230 --> 00:12:25,790
So...what did you think of your first funeral?

225
00:12:25,790 --> 00:12:28,980
Well, I don't want to be a jerk, but it was kind of a bummer.

226
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:33,820
Yeah, well, when I die, you can rent a bounce house.

227
00:12:34,930 --> 00:12:36,390
You think about dying?

228
00:12:36,390 --> 00:12:40,240
Well, I think more about if I'd have any regrets.

229
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,520
What would you regret?

230
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:44,440
Mm, you know, that I didn't travel more,

231
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:47,340
take more risks, learn another language.

232
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:49,290
You know Klingon.

233
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:51,200
That's true.

234
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,470
No, I meant that as a regret.

235
00:12:58,170 --> 00:13:00,440
- I just thought of one more. - What's that?

236
00:13:01,310 --> 00:13:05,360
I regret not saying "Yes" when you asked me to marry you.

237
00:13:05,950 --> 00:13:08,220
Well, it just wasn't the right time.

238
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:10,000
Yeah.

239
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,840
And this is also not the right time.

240
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:14,000
Do not propose.

241
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:15,170
What?

242
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:17,240
I know that face. That's your propose face.

243
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:21,000
I was not gonna propose. It's already two to one.

244
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:21,950
What's two to one?

245
00:13:21,950 --> 00:13:23,730
I proposed twice, you proposed once. Two to one.

246
00:13:23,730 --> 00:13:25,140
Oh, my... It's not a contest.

247
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,640
I don't know what you're upset about.

248
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,590
- I'm the one who's losing. - Okay.

249
00:13:29,550 --> 00:13:31,310
Fine. Would you feel better if I propose

250
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:32,500
so you could turn me down again?

251
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,930
Yeah, I think I would.

252
00:13:33,930 --> 00:13:36,880
Okay. Leonard, will you marry me?

253
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:40,180
No, don't you dare.

254
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:43,280
You reject me right now and tie things up.

255
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,670
It's just such a big decision.

256
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:48,970
I don't want to have any regrets.

257
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,710
Did you ever watch Professor Proton when you were a kid?

258
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:56,400
No.

259
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,690
My dad controlled the TV,

260
00:13:57,690 --> 00:13:59,410
so unless someone was a Texas Ranger,

261
00:13:59,410 --> 00:14:02,100
Jake or the Fatman, we didn't see it.

262
00:14:03,290 --> 00:14:05,350
I never watched him, either, but he seems to be the reason

263
00:14:05,350 --> 00:14:07,540
that Sheldon got interested in science.

264
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:09,420
Not me. I got into science

265
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,070
'cause I was always the smallest kid in school,

266
00:14:11,070 --> 00:14:13,020
so I thought if I became a scientist,

267
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:16,000
I could invent a formula that made me taller.

268
00:14:16,490 --> 00:14:17,950
That's cute.

269
00:14:17,950 --> 00:14:19,780
Yeah, I thought it was working for a while,

270
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,050
but then I found out my brother was just

271
00:14:21,050 --> 00:14:24,290
lowering the pencil marks on the door frame.

272
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:26,760
How about you?

273
00:14:27,150 --> 00:14:30,810
Oh, I guess it must have been back when I was in the Girl Sprouts.

274
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,700
Girl Sprouts?

275
00:14:33,700 --> 00:14:37,310
My mom made it up as an alternative to the Girl Scouts.

276
00:14:37,310 --> 00:14:38,680
She didn't want me selling cookies

277
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:41,690
on some street corner "Like a whore."

278
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,670
How did that get you into science?

279
00:14:47,670 --> 00:14:48,870
Oh, I went to the library

280
00:14:48,870 --> 00:14:52,230
and took out a book on biology to see what whores did.

281
00:14:55,850 --> 00:14:58,420
On the one hand, if I say yes...

282
00:14:59,570 --> 00:15:01,130
This isn't funny anymore.

283
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:02,730
Just say no so we're done with this.

284
00:15:02,730 --> 00:15:04,210
Will you marry me or not?

285
00:15:04,210 --> 00:15:08,210
Ooh, interesting. Did you just propose to me again?

286
00:15:09,230 --> 00:15:10,560
- No. - Really?

287
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,330
Because I just heard, "Will you marry me?"

288
00:15:12,330 --> 00:15:14,540
That's two proposals, one day.

289
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,940
Sounds like someone wants to spend the rest of her life

290
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:20,760
telling people how to spell the name Hofstadter.

291
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:24,140
You know what? Fine. Do whatever you want.

292
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:29,370
Penny, don't get upset.

293
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:30,850
Here.

294
00:15:30,850 --> 00:15:35,220
I love you, but, no, I will not marry you.

295
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:36,870
Thank you.

296
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:38,170
Now, about that second proposal.

297
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:40,100
On the one hand...

298
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:54,190
Where... where... where are we?

299
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:58,170
This is the swampland of Dagobah.

300
00:15:58,170 --> 00:16:02,150
It's where Luke was trained in the ways of the Jedi.

301
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:05,770
Too bad. I thought it was Florida.

302
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:16,250
When Obi-Wan came to Luke on this very spot,

303
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:19,330
he gave him all sorts of helpful advice.

304
00:16:19,330 --> 00:16:20,690
So, um...

305
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,850
what do you got for me?

306
00:16:28,090 --> 00:16:29,610
Always...

307
00:16:30,460 --> 00:16:32,880
get... get a prenup.

308
00:16:36,630 --> 00:16:38,290
That's it?

309
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:41,880
I thought there'd be more of a reason why you're here.

310
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:45,740
Well, why-why do you think I'm here?

311
00:16:46,180 --> 00:16:49,490
I suppose it has something to do with your recent passing.

312
00:16:49,490 --> 00:16:52,000
Is-is this the... the first time

313
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,770
you've lost, you know, someone close to you?

314
00:16:54,770 --> 00:16:56,940
Oh, no. No.

315
00:16:56,940 --> 00:17:00,930
I've already had to say good-bye to 11 Dr. Whos.

316
00:17:03,430 --> 00:17:07,250
Yeah, I've-I've outlived a few of my doctors, too.

317
00:17:09,390 --> 00:17:12,510
Of course, my grandfather died when I was five.

318
00:17:12,510 --> 00:17:15,560
My father died when I was 14.

319
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:18,360
I'm... I'm sorry about that.

320
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:20,190
And now you're gone, too.

321
00:17:22,110 --> 00:17:25,200
It's like all the men I've looked up to have gone away.

322
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:28,340
Well, you know, it's...

323
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:31,890
it's okay to... to be sad about them.

324
00:17:31,890 --> 00:17:36,310
Just... just make sure, you know, you appreciate

325
00:17:36,310 --> 00:17:40,200
those who... who are still there for you.

326
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:43,930
But I do appreciate them.

327
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,930
Well, then,

328
00:17:46,930 --> 00:17:49,620
what am I doing in a swamp...

329
00:17:54,050 --> 00:17:56,650
...dressed like Friar Tuck?

330
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:05,660
Appreciate them, Sheldon.

331
00:18:08,750 --> 00:18:10,160
Hey, buddy.

332
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:12,170
Heard you're having a rough day. You all right?

333
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:14,000
I'm okay.

334
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:17,250
How was the funeral?

335
00:18:18,570 --> 00:18:20,900
It was nice, you know.

336
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:22,720
A lot of people showed up,

337
00:18:23,450 --> 00:18:26,180
told some great stories about him.

338
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:28,770
Did you know that Arthur's son is a high school sci...?

339
00:18:45,990 --> 00:18:47,510
Hey, the guys are about to start Jedi.

340
00:18:47,510 --> 00:18:48,940
You want to go watch?

341
00:18:48,940 --> 00:18:50,290
I do.

342
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:55,480
After I make them go back and watch one through five first.

343
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:00,550
Sheldon, that-that'll take us all night.

344
00:19:00,550 --> 00:19:02,390
That's true.

345
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:04,760
Oh, it's a good thing I had a nap.

346
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,520
Boy, some of the physical comedy

347
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:15,390
with Jar Jar is a little tough to watch.

348
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:20,480
At least they toned him down in the second one.

349
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:23,260
Yeah, he is pretty stupid.

350
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:28,950
Hey, we can say it. You can't.

351
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:31,240
Hey, guys.

352
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,100
Happy Star Wars Day!

353
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,950
- A Death Star cake! - Yeah.

354
00:19:36,950 --> 00:19:38,590
We were hoping it might cheer you up.

355
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:40,200
And even though it meant we had to miss the movies,

356
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,800
we could still be part of the fun.

357
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:42,460
Well, you didn't miss anything.

358
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:44,250
We just started over.

359
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:46,590
Son of a bitch.

360
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:03,950
You're back.

361
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:06,110
Yeah, apparently, um,

362
00:20:06,110 --> 00:20:09,200
I'm here whenever... when-whenever you need me.

363
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:11,320
That's nice.

364
00:20:11,890 --> 00:20:13,960
May-Maybe for you.

365
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:18,590
Why do I need you now?

366
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:21,140
Well, as near as I could tell,

367
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:24,160
you-you fell asleep watching Star Wars,

368
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:28,470
and now you're-you're dreaming you're watching Star Wars.

369
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:30,370
So?

370
00:20:30,370 --> 00:20:33,300
I mean, don't-don't you see a problem there?

371
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,160
I mean, how-how

372
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:37,690
you're spending your limited time on Earth?

373
00:20:39,310 --> 00:20:41,650
Not at all.

374
00:20:41,650 --> 00:20:44,060
Okay, good luck to you.

